course: dictionary
lesson: 789
title: Words for rooms in a home
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A bedroom is a room for sleeping, with a bed in it. Bedroom is made of two smaller words, bed and room, joined together. When you meet a word like this, look for the small words inside it: they often give you the meaning.
explain: «A three-bedroom house» has three bedrooms. The number tells you how many rooms of this kind the house has. Here the word is used to count rooms, just as «a two-bedroom flat» has two.
explain: Read the words around bedroom to check its meaning. «Every evening she lies across Sam's bedroom door» tells you the bedroom has a door, and that Sam sleeps or spends time there. «Charging devices outside the bedroom» shows that the bedroom is a room you can be inside or outside of.
fact: A bedroom is a room for sleeping, with a bed in it.
fact: Bedroom is a noun, and its plural is bedrooms.
fact: Bed and room are two smaller words joined to make bedroom.
fact: «A three-bedroom house» has three bedrooms, so the number tells you how many.
fact: Phrases you may hear are «my bedroom», «spare bedroom» (a room kept for guests) and «three-bedroom house».
exercise: What is a bedroom? | A shed in the garden for tools | A room for cooking and eating | A room where you keep the car | *A room for sleeping, with a bed in it
exercise: «A three-bedroom house» has how many bedrooms? | Thirty | *Three | Two | Four
exercise: In «the Rat, used to a breezy river bedroom, feels sleepy and shut in», what does breezy suggest? | Dark and very small | Full of loud music | *Fresh air moving through the room | Locked with a key
test: In «Charging devices outside the bedroom removes the temptation to play at night», where are the devices charged? | Inside the bedroom, next to the bed | In the kitchen cupboard | *Outside the bedroom | Under the stairs
test: What two smaller words make up bedroom? | bread and room | *bed and room | bed and roof | bee and room
exam: Which sentence uses bedroom correctly? | I cooked my bedroom for tea | I swam in my bedroom at the baths | I read my bedroom in the library | *I tidied my bedroom before tea
